{
  "description": "Frozen number-to-string semantics for SVG attribute values. `input` is a canonical decimal string; parse it to a 64-bit float (JS Number(input) / Rust f64::from_str) before formatting. Any emitter implementation must reproduce every expected column byte-for-byte.",
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "string",
      "algorithm": "ECMAScript String(number) (shortest round-trip representation; exponent notation outside [1e-6, 1e21); -0 formats as \"0\")",
      "expectedField": "expected",
      "sites": [
        "packages/core/src/transform.ts transformToSvg (translate/rotate/scale operands via local formatSvgNumber, which is observably identical to String)",
        "crates/boundsvg/src/svg_emit/emitter.rs (MISSING_GLYPH_OPACITY constant interpolation)",
        "crates/boundsvg/src/svg_emit/emitter.rs (integer filter-region percentages x/y/width/height)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "round2-string",
      "algorithm": "String(Math.round(n * 100) / 100); NaN/Infinity throw before formatting; when rounding overflows to Infinity near Number.MAX_VALUE the unrounded value formats via String(n)",
      "expectedField": "expectedRound2",
      "sites": [
        "packages/core/src/svg/utils.ts formatNumber (precision default 2)",
        "crates/boundsvg/src/svg_emit/emitter.rs (viewBox/width/height, rect/image/path/nested-svg/shape geometry, rounded-rect and clip path data, stroke widths, group opacity, debug overlays)",
        "crates/boundsvg/src/svg_emit/emitter.rs (clipPath geometry and radii, feDropShadow/feGaussianBlur/feMorphology/feOffset parameters)",
        "crates/boundsvg/src/svg_emit/emitter.rs (gradient stop offset percentages)",
        "packages/core/src/shape/serialize-region.ts (region path point coordinates)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "round4-string",
      "algorithm": "String(Math.round(n * 10000) / 10000); same non-finite and overflow behavior as round2-string",
      "expectedField": "expectedRound4",
      "sites": [
        "crates/boundsvg/src/svg_emit/emitter.rs linearGradient defs (x1/y1/x2/y2 unit-space endpoints)"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "transformToSvg formats non-finite values via String (e.g. \"NaN\") instead of throwing; upstream validation prevents non-finite transform fields in practice, so no fixture case exercises it.",
    "packages/core/src/path/utils.ts formatPathNumber is a fourth, near-round2 variant (no non-finite guard, no overflow fallback: Number.MAX_VALUE formats as \"Infinity\"; redundant -0 normalization). Its only caller transformPathData has no production call sites today - it must not be used as the emit-path reference."
  ],
